let context = CIContext(options: nil)
let cgImage = context.createCGImage(outputImage, from: outputImage.extent)!
let processedImage = UIImage(cgImage: cgImage)
```
Step 5: Address environmental variables
Environmental variables such as ambient noise and weather can impact the final outcome of the photos. To address these variables, you can use Swift code to adjust the camera settings accordingly. Here is an example of Swift code that adjusts the ISO and shutter speed based on the ambient light:
```
let lightLevel = UIScreen.main.brightness
let iso = captureDevice.activeFormat.maxISO - Double(lightLevel) * (captureDevice.activeFormat.maxISO - captureDevice.activeFormat.minISO)
let shutterSpeed = 1.0 / (2.0 * lightLevel + 0.25)
