    return 0;
}
```
The above code snippet uses Boost.Asio to establish a connection to a server using a 5G network, send a message, and receive a response. The speed and reliability of the 5G network allows for faster communication between the client and the server, resulting in a more seamless user experience.
In addition to faster connectivity, advancements in communication technology have also improved communication security. For example, the use of encryption protocols such as SSL/TLS has become more widespread, ensuring that sensitive information is protected from malicious attacks. Here's an example of how OpenSSL can be used to demonstrate the impact of encryption on communication security:
```c++
#include <openssl/ssl.h>
#include <openssl/err.h>
#include <iostream>
int main()
{
    SSL_library_init();
    SSL_CTX* ssl_ctx = SSL_CTX_new(TLS_client_method());
    // Establish a secure connection to a server
    int socket_fd = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);
    struct sockaddr_in server_addr;
    server_addr.sin_family = AF_INET;
    server_addr.sin_port = htons(443);
    inet_pton(AF_INET, "example.com", &server_addr.sin_addr);
    connect(socket_fd, (struct sockaddr*)&server_addr, sizeof(server_addr));
    SSL* ssl = SSL_new(ssl_ctx);
    SSL_set_fd(ssl, socket_fd);
    SSL_connect(ssl);
    // Send a message to the server
    std::string message = "Hello, server!";
    SSL_write(ssl, message.c_str(), message.length());
    // Receive a response from the server
    char buffer[1024];
    SSL_read(ssl, buffer, sizeof(buffer));
    // Print the response
    std::cout << "Response: " << buffer << std::endl;
    // Clean up
    SSL_shutdown(ssl);
    SSL_free(ssl);
    SSL_CTX_free(ssl_ctx);
    close(socket_fd);
    return 0;
}
```
The above code snippet uses OpenSSL to establish a secure connection to a server using SSL/TLS encryption, send a message, and receive a response. The use of encryption ensures that the message sent between the client and the server is protected from eavesdropping and tampering, improving communication security.
