public class PrimeAndSumOfDigits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int num = 19;
        int sumOfDigits = 0;
        boolean isPrime = true;
        // Check if the number is prime
        for (int i = 2; i <= num / 2; i++) {
            if (num % i == 0) {
                isPrime = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        // Calculate the sum of digits
        while (num > 0) {
            sumOfDigits += num % 10;
            num /= 10;
        }
        // Check if the sum of digits is a multiple of 3
        boolean isSumOfDigitsMultipleOf3 = sumOfDigits % 3 == 0;
        // Output 1 for prime and the sum of digits is a multiple of 3, 0 otherwise
        if (isPrime && isSumOfDigitsMultipleOf3) {
            System.out.println(1);
        } else {
            System.out.println(0);
        }
    }
}
```
This code first checks if the number is prime by dividing it by all numbers from 2 to half of the number. If the number is divisible by any of these numbers, it is not prime. If the number is prime, it then calculates the sum of its digits by repeatedly dividing the number by 10 and adding the remainder to the sum. Finally, it checks if the sum of digits is a multiple of 3 and outputs 1 if the number is prime and the sum of digits is a multiple of 3, and 0 otherwise.

